 ## Overview
-Wavelet-based Volume Rendering is a technique that compresses volumetric data using wavelet transforms to enable efficient storage and rendering, particularly for large-scale or time-varying datasets [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high memory bandwidth and storage requirements by representing the volume in a frequency domain where coefficients can be pruned or encoded [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from its sibling [Laplacian Pyramid Volume Rendering](2261-laplacian-pyramid-volume-rendering.md) by its use of orthogonal or biorthogonal wavelet bases (such as Haar or Daubechies) which provide multi-resolution analysis with better frequency localization, whereas Laplacian pyramids use fixed Gaussian filters [S1, unofficial][S3].
+Wavelet-based Volume Rendering is a technique that compresses volumetric data using wavelet transforms to enable efficient storage and rendering, particularly for large-scale or time-varying datasets [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of high memory bandwidth and storage requirements by representing the volume in a frequency domain where coefficients can be pruned or encoded [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from its sibling [Laplacian Pyramid Volume Rendering](2261-laplacian-pyramid-volume-rendering.md) by its use of orthogonal or biorthogonal wavelet bases (such as Haar or Daubechies) which provide multi-resolution analysis with better frequency localization, whereas Laplacian pyramids use fixed Gaussian filters [S3].
 
