 ## Operating characteristics
-* **Time Complexity:** Depends on the reconstruction method. Point-wise reconstruction has complexity $O(m^3 n^3)$, while block-wise reconstruction reduces this to $O(3mn^3)$, offering an efficiency factor of $k = m^2/3$ [S3]. Wavelet splatting Method 1 has complexity decaying with $2^j$ per scale, while Method 2 decays with $2^{3j}$ [S4, unofficial].
